    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0896" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg786"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Peraza.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 19,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    received a dispatch from our minister at London, reporting that, in compliance
                    with my instructions, of the transmission of which I advised you on the 2d
                    instant, he had an interview with Lord Salisbury in regard to the renewal of
                    diplomatic relations between Venezuela and Great Britain and the settlement of
                    the boundary dispute by arbitration.</p>
                <p>After listening to the views of this Government, His Lordship informed Mr.
                    Lincoln that he desired to consult with the colonial office before replying to
                    his suggestions.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
